1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:05,688
Two people invest the same hundred dollars a month. One ends up with twice as much.

2
00:00:06,038 --> 00:00:11,362
Alex starts at twenty. Sam waits until thirty. Both keep going until sixty five.

3
00:00:11,712 --> 00:00:18,117
Say they both earn about seven percent a year in an index fund. That's a long term average, not a promise.

4
00:00:18,467 --> 00:00:23,743
Sam puts in forty two thousand dollars, and ends up with about a hundred and eighty thousand.

5
00:00:24,093 --> 00:00:29,680
Alex puts in just twelve thousand more, and ends up with about three hundred and seventy nine thousand.

6
00:00:30,030 --> 00:00:38,267
That extra money is compound growth. Your returns start earning returns of their own, and ten extra years lets that snowball roll.

7
00:00:38,617 --> 00:00:43,016
So you don't need a lot of money. You need time. Start small, and start now.
